WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:14.752
Sara spent a terrible first night in the attic.

2
00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:16.733
Her bed felt hard.

3
00:00:18.395 --> 00:00:22.158
The room was pitch black, and the wind howled over the roof.

4
00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:25.520
But there was something worse.

5
00:00:26.761 --> 00:00:29.744
Sara heard scratching and squeaking in the walls.

6
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:32.845
She knew what that meant.

7
00:00:34.266 --> 00:00:37.449
Becky had told her about the mice and rats living in the attic.

8
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.913
Sara pulled the thin blanket over her head and tried to sleep.

9
00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:44.495
"My papa is dead!"

10
00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:46.476
she kept whispering to herself.

11
00:00:46.496 --> 00:00:48.818
"My papa is dead!"

12
00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:57.125
The next morning when Sara went down to breakfast, she saw that someone was sitting in her seat

13
00:00:57.205 --> 00:00:58.206
next to Miss Minchin.

14
00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:00.368
It was Lavinia.

15
00:01:03.236 --> 00:01:08.338
"Sara, you will begin your new duties at once," Miss Minchin said coldly.

16
00:01:08.358 --> 00:01:12.059
"Sit with the younger girls and make sure they behave.

17
00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.439
You should have been here earlier.

18
00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:16.800
Lottie has already spilled her tea."

19
00:01:18.781 --> 00:01:21.161
Sara's duties at breakfast were only the beginning.

20
00:01:22.562 --> 00:01:26.743
The headmistress knew that Sara was smart and could be sent on complicated errands.

21
00:01:28.524 --> 00:01:29.584
She could even pay bills.

22
00:01:30.792 --> 00:01:34.554
So soon Sara was sent out at all times of day and in any weather.

23
00:01:35.815 --> 00:01:37.896
Sara worked hard and didn't complain.

24
00:01:39.177 --> 00:01:41.579
For a while she thought this would make everyone like her.

25
00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:45.181
But the other servants were delighted at her downfall.

26
00:01:46.401 --> 00:01:48.543
The maids gave her the worst jobs to do.

27
00:01:50.224 --> 00:01:51.905
The cook always scolded her.

28
00:01:52.925 --> 00:01:57.248
It was convenient for them to have a new servant to blame for every problem at the school.

29
00:01:58.588 --> 00:02:01.290
Of course Sara no longer went to any classes.

30
00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.935
"I'm afraid I'll forget everything I've learned," she said to Miss Minchin.

31
00:02:06.955 --> 00:02:12.940
"Well, you could use the schoolroom at night," the headmistress said grudgingly.

32
00:02:14.261 --> 00:02:18.044
Each night Sara sat alone in the schoolroom, reading old books.

33
00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:23.148
As time passed, her clothes became shabbier.

34
00:02:26.132 --> 00:02:29.273
Miss Minchin told the other girls not to talk to Sara anymore.

35
00:02:30.553 --> 00:02:32.934
Sara now had to eat downstairs in the kitchen.

36
00:02:35.315 --> 00:02:40.396
Each day she worked hard, trudging through the wet streets carrying parcels and baskets.

37
00:02:41.716 --> 00:02:45.257
Her heart was breaking, but she was determined not to show it.

38
00:02:45.277 --> 00:02:49.838
"Soldiers don't complain," she reminded herself.

39
00:02:49.858 --> 00:02:52.879
"So I will not either.

40
00:02:53.399 --> 00:02:55.320
I will pretend I am at war."

41
00:02:57.408 --> 00:02:59.409
Becky was still kind to Sara.

42
00:03:00.549 --> 00:03:03.230
Every day she helped Sara to dress and undress.

43
00:03:04.631 --> 00:03:08.633
But Becky was so busy with her own chores, she didn't have much time to talk.

44
00:03:10.974 --> 00:03:13.555
One day Ermengarde saw Sara coming down the hall.

45
00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:18.217
Sara was carrying a pile of clothes to be mended.

46
00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:22.998
Sara looked so pale and poor, Ermengarde wasn't sure what to say.

47
00:03:24.279 --> 00:03:26.440
So she blurted out the first thing she thought of.

48
00:03:27.572 --> 00:03:30.093
"Oh oh How are you, Sara?

49
00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:31.793
Are you very unhappy?"

50
00:03:31.813 --> 00:03:34.434
"What do you think?"

51
00:03:34.994 --> 00:03:36.475
Sara suddenly felt annoyed.

52
00:03:37.455 --> 00:03:39.936
She marched past Ermengarde without another word.

53
00:03:39.956 --> 00:03:44.477
"Ermengarde is just like the others," Sara said to herself.

54
00:03:45.618 --> 00:03:47.518
"She doesn't really want to talk to me."

55
00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:53.100
Whenever they met after that, Sara always looked the other way.

56
00:03:54.348 --> 00:03:57.571
And Ermengarde always felt too awkward and embarrassed to speak.

57
00:03:58.632 --> 00:04:01.054
But things had changed greatly for Ermengarde too.

58
00:04:02.055 --> 00:04:05.157
Without Sara, Ermengarde was lonely and miserable.

59
00:04:06.778 --> 00:04:12.823
She constantly made mistakes during lessons, and she spent hours by herself, just staring out the window.

60
00:04:15.185 --> 00:04:19.469
One night when Sara returned to the attic, she saw a flicker of light under her door.

61
00:04:19.489 --> 00:04:22.912
"That's strange," she thought.

62
00:04:26.356 --> 00:04:27.838
She opened the door slowly.

63
00:04:28.498 --> 00:04:29.839
Inside was Ermengarde.

64
00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.283
She was sitting on the footstool, dressed in her nightgown and a red shawl.

65
00:04:34.303 --> 00:04:37.446
"Ermengarde!" cried Sara.

66
00:04:37.466 --> 00:04:39.427
"What are you doing here?"

67
00:04:41.189 --> 00:04:43.190
Ermengarde stumbled up from the footstool.

68
00:04:44.211 --> 00:04:46.933
She shuffled across the attic in her bedroom slippers.

69
00:04:48.174 --> 00:04:50.356
Her eyes and nose were pink from crying.

70
00:04:50.376 --> 00:04:55.760
"I couldn't bear it anymore," said Ermengarde.

71
00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.843
"You may be able to live without me, but I can't live without you.

72
00:04:59.483 --> 00:05:00.724
Why won't you speak to me?"

73
00:05:00.745 --> 00:05:04.187
"I thought you didn't like me.

74
00:05:05.248 --> 00:05:09.432
Everything is different now—I'm a servant," Sara reminded her.

75
00:05:09.452 --> 00:05:13.155
"I don't care about that," said Ermengarde.

76
00:05:13.175 --> 00:05:15.537
"Can't we be best friends again?"

77
00:05:15.557 --> 00:05:18.560
"Oh yes!"

78
00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.062
Sara rushed into Ermengarde's arms.

79
00:05:21.082 --> 00:05:23.024
"I've missed you!"

80
00:05:25.864 --> 00:05:27.205
Ermengarde looked around the room.

81
00:05:27.225 --> 00:05:31.547
"Sara, how can you stand living here?"

82
00:05:33.549 --> 00:05:35.129
Sara looked around the room too.

83
00:05:35.149 --> 00:05:40.793
"Other people have lived in worse places," she replied.

84
00:05:40.813 --> 00:05:45.996
"Think of the prisoners in the Bastille prison during the French Revolution."

85
00:05:46.016 --> 00:05:48.857
"You could make up a story!"

86
00:05:49.358 --> 00:05:50.138
said Ermengarde.

87
00:05:50.158 --> 00:05:53.040
"That's a wonderful idea!"

88
00:05:54.908 --> 00:05:59.229
Sara felt her imagination stirring for the first time since her father had died.

89
00:05:59.249 --> 00:06:02.710
"I could pretend that Miss Minchin is the jailer.

90
00:06:04.131 --> 00:06:06.531
And Becky is the prisoner in the next cell!"

91
00:06:07.712 --> 00:06:11.913
Sara's eyes were glowing, and she was already starting to look more like her old self.

92
00:06:11.933 --> 00:06:18.094
"I will tell myself the stories, and it will be a great comfort to me!"

93
00:06:18.114 --> 00:06:22.215
"I'll creep up here every night to hear the stories too!"

94
00:06:22.656 --> 00:06:23.656
Ermengarde promised.
